# Frontend Language Policy (English Only)

- Any user-facing frontend text in `apps/web/src` must be written in English.
- Do not add Spanish (or mixed-language) labels, buttons, placeholders, toasts, helper text, empty states, or error copy in the frontend.
- When editing existing UI, convert nearby non-English strings to English for consistency.
- Route labels and navigation copy shown to users must also be English.

## Examples

- Bad: `"Volver"`, `"Mis escenarios"`, `"Enviado a revision"`
- Good: `"Back"`, `"My scenarios"`, `"Submitted for review"`
